  "interpretation": [
    "All four E3 warm medians are slower than E2 in this bounded run. Only Portra UHD E2 has a lower median than named R-B1; the other E2 cases are slower.",
    "E3 adds a second full-width float ring, extra materialization and AOT work; UHD halation/log calls are seven for five output bands. Exact exclusive stage GPU time remains unknown.",
    "E3 caches post-halation LogExposure, not persistent individual multiscale fields. It still waits per output band and does not introduce device concurrency.",
    "E2 keeps the conservative producer margin; E3 uses per-edge support and a second cache. Necessary demand/batch changes are part of this design comparison, not an isolated causal test of stage count.",
    "Four main cases are tuning data. One round per arm, changing thermal state 0/1, background load and unfrozen reference stability prevent a general speed claim. Docker was not quit.",
    "Two/three-stage output hashes differ within the original pixel tolerance; all finite values and alpha checks pass. Traced E3 hashes match normal E3.",
    "Device peaks include cold start and both rings/scratch/pool. They are not the formal named-edge locality or retention non-regression result."
  ],
